// # app — Application Bridges (mirrors std/app)
//
// Logline: The "outside" bridges — FFI / xlang for linking against non-C targets, HITL for human-in-the-loop approval, telemetry for metrics + event bus, the OTP-style actor runtime (the only oodar-native execution model), and the stdout/stderr print bridge.
//
// Setup: xlang/ is the FFI surface (cap-gated, signature-verified). hitl/ is the TTY-based approval primitive (env-gated, fail-closed). telemetry/ is the counter export + event bus (subscribes to crypto/FS events via constructor). actor/ is the actor + channel + thread + closure primitives. io/ is the stdout/stderr print family (moved from fs/io/ in v2.2.0 — it's an output app bridge, not a host primitive).
//
// Beats:
//   1. xlang/ffi.c, ffi_sec.c — dlopen/dlsym and the cap-gated signature-verified wrapper.
//   2. xlang/xlang.c — cross-language dispatch.
//   3. hitl/hitl.c — verify_human (TTY-based, OODA_HITL_ALLOW-gated).
//   4. telemetry/event.c, event.h — the event bus (oo_event_emit, oo_event_subscribe).
//   5. telemetry/metrics.c — the counter export (subscribes to events at constructor).
//   6. actor/actor.c, channel.c, thread.c, closure.c — the actor runtime (OTP-style spawn/send/recv/restart/supervise).
//   7. io/print.c — stdout/stderr print family (oo_print_str, oo_print_int, oo_print_bool, oo_print_double, oo_println, oo_eprint_str, oo_eprintln).
//
// ──▓▓ app ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: FFI is the highest-risk attack surface — every load is cap + signature gated ::
